    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4017071a_311bdffa",
        "filename": "android/prebuilt.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 236,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-17T02:35:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t srcsSupplier added in this CL? Then there\u0027s no previous behaviour. It\u0027d be simpler if it can always be assumed to be set, and just crash if not. It may perhaps make sense to allow it to return nil, although judging from the comment you added there\u0027s no difference between nil and an empty array, so I think it\u0027d be better to not allow that either.\n\nIf there are code paths that need a dummy srcsSupplier that only returns an empty array then so be it; less tolerance for different representations is still better.",
      "parentUuid": "52823e87_627a30b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 236,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 236,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "1e7a912867e68b82c479fd9f4aaefe81f965c9f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "83fba803_a4f401ba",
        "filename": "android/prebuilt.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 236,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-17T09:55:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The srcsSupplier is new but it replaces srcs and srcProps. The behavior of srcsSupplier here is the same as the previous behavior around srcs and srcProps. i.e. this will not fail if the Init... method has not been called.\n\nI don\u0027t know whether it was intentional for this method to behave that way. Removing the check against nil does not cause any unit tests to fail but it may cause issues in the actual build.\nI am going to submit as it is because it has not made things worse and we can always clean it up in future if it becomes necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "4017071a_311bdffa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 236,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 236,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "1e7a912867e68b82c479fd9f4aaefe81f965c9f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33cf5d52_afb4b1a3",
        "filename": "android/prebuilt.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 236,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-17T12:23:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The srcsSupplier is new but it replaces srcs \n\nNo. You\u0027ve replaced srcs with the *return value* from srcsSupplier. There\u0027s still an opportunity to avoid dealing with srcsSupplier itself being null, without affecting the old logic.\n\nIn fact, it looks possible to do away with the srcsSupplier pointer entirely by splitting Prebuilt into an interface and a base struct, and instead let InitPrebuiltModuleWithSrcSupplier take the implementation struct. I wouldn\u0027t necessarily go that far, though.",
      "parentUuid": "83fba803_a4f401ba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 236,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 236,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "1e7a912867e68b82c479fd9f4aaefe81f965c9f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2652f7e9_8c4bf776",
        "filename": "android/prebuilt.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 236,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-17T13:46:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e You\u0027ve replaced srcs with the *return value* from srcsSupplier.\n\nsrcs is *[]string which is equivalent to srcsSupplier.\n*srcs is []string which is the return value from srcsSupplier.\n\nIf I don\u0027t allow for srcsSupplier to be nil I change the behavior of the usePrebuilt() method as it will now fail if an Init... method had not been called on the Prebuilt. That would be equivalent to the previous code failing if srcs was nil and srcProps was not valid.\n\nNow, it may be that change is ok (it certainly doesn\u0027t break any unit tests) but it is a change in behavior which I wanted to avoid as much as possible in this change. The purpose of this change was simply to allow for custom suppliers to be added not to change existing behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "33cf5d52_afb4b1a3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 236,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 236,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "1e7a912867e68b82c479fd9f4aaefe81f965c9f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    }
